Title: Last Call

INT. ROADHOUSE BAR - NIGHT

Smoke hangs under the neon. MARA (20s) wipes the counter.

A BURLY MAN (50s), tattooed forearms, shaved head, leather vest, nurses a beer at the end of the bar. Gruff and watchful.

MARA
Who's the big guy? BURLY MAN hasn't said a word all night.

JIM
Leave him be.

BURLY MAN
Another.

EXT. PARKING LOT - NIGHT

BURLY MAN lights a cigarette by his pickup truck. He checks a folded photograph.

BURLY MAN
Go home, kid!

BIG JIM
You heard him.

INT. ROADHOUSE BAR - LATER

BURLY MAN sets the photograph on the counter in front of MARA.

BURLY MAN
She looked like you.

MARA
Who?

BURLY MAN
My daughter.
